-- 1) 454 → KFUPM Scholarship (Full MS & PhD Scholarship), rel 10, upcoming, 2026-12-15/fixed
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'KFUPM Scholarship (Full MS & PhD Scholarship)', provider = 'King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals', coverage_type = 'Full Tuition + Stipend', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'The scholarship is awarded through graduate admission, which runs in windows announced by the College of Graduate & Interdisciplinary Studies (CGIS). The next window for MS (Thesis-Based) and PhD programmes runs from 1 November to 15 December 2026 - the CGIS homepage showed it as upcoming when this record was verified - and applications are submitted online via the CGIS portal during the window. Distinguished full-time applicants are considered for the full scholarship within the admission process; note the higher GPA bar for scholarship applicants at master''s level.', deadline_date = '2026-12-15', deadline_type = 'fixed', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's", "PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["Full-time graduate programmes in engineering and the sciences at KFUPM: scholarships are offered for ALL PhD programmes (including the PhD - Direct Entry route from a bachelor's degree) and for select thesis-based MS programmes that do not have corresponding doctoral tracks"]$j$, eligible_countries = $j$["Open to Saudi and international graduate applicants admitted full-time; air tickets are provided for international students only"]$j$, min_gpa = 3.00, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The KFUPM Scholarship is King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals' full graduate scholarship: distinguished graduate applicants who demonstrate exceptional qualifications and performance with a high GPA can be admitted as full-time MS or PhD students with a full scholarship. Its coverage is explicit on the official pages - scholarships are offered for all PhD programmes, including the PhD - Direct Entry route that takes strong bachelor's graduates straight into a five-year doctorate (with the full scholarship provided for the first four years), and for select thesis-based MS programmes that do not have corresponding doctoral tracks. The package is genuinely comprehensive: a stipend paid according to category (the university does not publish the category amounts on the pages read, so no figure is recorded here), free furnished air-conditioned on-campus housing including utilities and maintenance, air tickets for international students, medical and dental care, subsidized meals, free textbooks and - the headline - tuition-free study with no tuition fee at all. On top of that come opportunities to work as a research assistant (RA-MS/RA-PhD) on research projects with additional financial benefits, funding to participate in conferences under certain conditions, and the main library and departmental resource centres on a safe campus with recreational facilities, including a private beach. All courses at KFUPM are taught in English, which is why English test scores are part of admission (IELTS 6.0 at master's level, 6.5 for the PhD routes, or the listed TOEFL/Duolingo equivalents). Admission runs in windows announced by the College of Graduate & Interdisciplinary Studies - the next MS (Thesis-Based) and PhD window runs 1 November to 15 December 2026 - and scholarship consideration is built into that admission process rather than being a separate competition. KFUPM's undergraduate full scholarship for international students is a separate scheme (catalogue record 608); this record covers the graduate scholarship only.$desc$, requirements = $req$The scholarship rides on graduate admission, so you apply for the degree - during an announced CGIS application window (next: 1 November-15 December 2026 for MS (Thesis-Based) and PhD) - and distinguished full-time admits receive it. Academic gates are published and uniform: a minimum GPA of 3.00 on a 4.00 scale (for the MS this is explicitly the bar for scholarship applicants, versus 2.50 for non-scholarship applicants; PhD applicants need 3.00 in both the B.S. and M.S.; Direct-Entry PhD needs 3.00 in the B.S.). Degrees must fit the route: a four-year bachelor's in engineering or science for the MS and Direct-Entry PhD, plus an M.S. in engineering or science for the standard PhD, in the proposed field or with evidence of suitable background. English proficiency: TOEFL 520 (PBT) / 190 (CBT) / 70 (iBT), IELTS 6.0 or Duolingo 105 for the MS; TOEFL 550 / 213 / 80, IELTS 6.5 or Duolingo 120 for the PhD and Direct-Entry PhD - waived for KFUPM graduates and for graduates from the USA, Canada, UK, Australia and New Zealand; TOEFL scores go to institution code 0868. Two letters of recommendation (preferably from faculty who taught you, submitted through the online recommendation system) and any additional departmental or university requirements complete the file; official transcripts and degree certificates are required. The university is explicit that meeting the minima does not guarantee admission - decisions weigh the whole application and programme capacity. The GPA minimum is a single published figure so it is recorded (3.00/4.00); the IELTS minimum differs by level (6.0 vs 6.5) so min_ielts is left empty and the figures are stated here.$req$, website_url = 'https://cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/admission/kfupm-scholarship', source_url = 'https://cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/admission/kfupm-scholarship', application_url = 'https://cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-28 (cleanup pass 116) from King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals official pages fetched the same day: the CGIS 'KFUPM Scholarship' page (cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/admission/kfupm-scholarship - distinguished graduate applicants with a high GPA admitted as full-time MS or PhD students with a full scholarship; 'We offer scholarships for all PhD programs and PhD - Direct Entry Programs'; benefits: stipend according to category, free furnished air-conditioned on-campus housing with utilities and maintenance, air tickets only for International students, medical/dental care, subsidized meals, RA-PhD opportunity, free study with no tuition fee, conference funding under certain conditions, research-project work with financial benefits, library and department resource centers, safe and secure environment, recreational facilities including a private beach, free textbooks; Direct PhD lasts five years with the full scholarship for the first four years; SAR fee table for self-sponsored students), the main-site 'Tuition costs and Scholarships' page for international students (kfupm.edu.sa/study/international-students/fees-and-scholarships - comprehensive scholarships for all PhD programs and select MS programs that don't have corresponding doctoral tracks, with the same benefit list framed for international graduate students; all courses taught in English; undergraduate international students separately receive a full scholarship with tuition waived - that undergraduate scheme is catalogue record 608 and is NOT this record), the CGIS admission-requirements page and the main-site MS/PhD programme page (GPA 3.00/4.00 minimum - explicitly 'For Scholarship Applicants' at MS level vs 2.50 non-scholarship, and 3.00 in both degrees for PhD / in the B.S. for Direct Entry; English TOEFL 520/190/70 or IELTS 6.0 or Duolingo 105 for MS, TOEFL 550/213/80 or IELTS 6.5 or Duolingo 120 for PhD routes, waived for KFUPM graduates and graduates from the USA, Canada, UK, Australia and New Zealand, TOEFL code 0868; two recommendation letters via the online system; official transcripts/certificates; minima do not guarantee admission), and the CGIS homepage (MS (Thesis-Based) and PhD application window: starts 01 November 2026, ends 15 December 2026, shown as upcoming/closed between cycles; Apply button to the CGIS portal, tracking at nabegh.kfupm.edu.sa - application_url set to the CGIS portal the Apply button targets). The previously stored URL (postgrad.kfupm.edu.sa/scholarships) no longer loads; the record is re-anchored to the CGIS scholarship page that now carries the scheme, and the title now leads with the official scheme name ('KFUPM Scholarship'). deadline_date 2026-12-15 ('fixed') is the published end of the next application window; status 'upcoming' because the window opens 1 November 2026. Award stored as NULL (SAR, 'variable', 'variable'): the stipend is 'according to category' and no category amount is published on the pages read - aggregator figures were not imported; amount_usd_value 0 (non-USD). min_gpa 3.00 recorded because one official scale-unambiguous figure (3.00 on a 4.00 scale) gates scholarship consideration on every route; min_ielts NULL because the English minimum differs by level (6.0 MS, 6.5 PhD). university_scholarships row 598 synced (us 67 belongs to the undergraduate record 608, untouched); source 2553 (exclusive to this record; target URL pre-checked free) repointed from the bare kfupm.edu.sa homepage to the CGIS scholarship page. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 behind a dead URL with no terms read.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'SAR', award_period = 'variable', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Full scholarship for full-time graduate students: stipend according to category, no tuition fee, free furnished on-campus housing (utilities and maintenance included), air tickets for international students, medical/dental care, subsidized meals and free textbooks; offered for all PhD programmes (incl. Direct-Entry PhD, funded for the first 4 of its 5 years) and select thesis-based MS programmes without doctoral tracks', tuition_coverage = 'Tuition-free study (no tuition fee) for scholarship holders, alongside the stipend and housing package; RA-MS/RA-PhD research-assistant opportunities and conference funding under conditions.', english_requirements = 'MS: TOEFL 520 PBT / 190 CBT / 70 iBT, or IELTS 6.0, or Duolingo 105. PhD and Direct-Entry PhD: TOEFL 550 / 213 / 80, or IELTS 6.5, or Duolingo 120. Waived for KFUPM graduates and graduates from the USA, Canada, UK, Australia and New Zealand; TOEFL institution code 0868. (min_ielts not recorded - the minimum differs by level.)', required_documents = $j$["Online graduate admission application via the CGIS portal during an announced window (MS (Thesis-Based) and PhD: 1 November - 15 December 2026)", "Official transcripts and degree certificates (GPA 3.00/4.00 minimum for scholarship consideration)", "English test scores at the published minima (TOEFL sent to code 0868; or IELTS / Duolingo), unless waived for KFUPM or English-speaking-country graduates", "Two letters of recommendation, preferably from faculty who taught the applicant, submitted through the online recommendation system", "Any additional departmental or university admission requirements for the chosen programme"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"cycle": "MS (Thesis-Based) and PhD admission window (scholarship considered within admission)", "opens": "2026-11-01", "deadline": "2026-12-15", "status": "upcoming"}, {"pattern": "Graduate admissions run in periodic windows announced on the CGIS homepage, with separate windows for project-based MS programmes; the full scholarship is awarded to distinguished full-time admits rather than through a separate application"}]$json$ WHERE id = 454 RETURNING id, title, source_reliability;

-- 2) 859 → RETIRED as a multi-institution application portal (not a single scholarship)
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$RETIRED on 2026-10-28 (cleanup pass 116) as a multi-institution application portal rather than a single scholarship. The stored URL (studyinsaudi.moe.gov.sa) did not load for the fetcher, so the platform was read at its official studyinsaudi.sa address (English homepage fetched 2026-10-28; Saudi government site registered with the Digital Government Authority): the 'Study in Saudi Arabia' platform is the Ministry of Education's gateway where students complete a profile and apply to academic programmes across more than 50 public and private Saudi universities, under three distinct funding routes - Fully Funded Scholarships, Partially Funded Scholarships and Self-Funded Programs - with award terms set by each institution and programme, and portal-wide application windows that vary by semester. The stored title itself conceded the point ('Official Scholarship Portal (multiple award types)'). Under the catalogue's standing rule, portal/directory rows are retired rather than displayed as single scholarships; individually verified Saudi schemes are carried as institution-level records (e.g. record 454 KFUPM graduate scholarship, rewritten at reliability 10 in this pass, and record 608 KFUPM undergraduate scholarship). This row had no linked sources and no university_scholarships rows.$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 859 RETURNING id, title, is_active;

-- 3) Source repoint (2553 exclusive to 454; target URL pre-checked free)
UPDATE sources SET url = 'https://cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/admission/kfupm-scholarship', title = 'KFUPM Scholarship — cgis.kfupm.edu.sa', accessed_at = now(), is_verified = true WHERE id = 2553 RETURNING id, url;

-- 4) university_scholarships: sync 598 (454 at uni 69)
UPDATE university_scholarships SET scholarship_name = 'KFUPM Scholarship (Full MS & PhD Scholarship)', availability_status = 'international_students', funding_type = 'Full scholarship: stipend according to category + no tuition fee + free furnished on-campus housing + air tickets (international students) + medical/dental care + subsidized meals + free textbooks', max_scholarship = 'Full ride: tuition-free study + stipend by category + free furnished housing + air tickets + medical/dental care', covers_tuition = true, covers_living_expenses = true, valued_aspect = 'Exceptional academic qualifications and research potential in engineering and the sciences (GPA 3.00/4.00 minimum for scholarship applicants)', eligibility_notes = 'Full-time thesis-based MS (scholarships for select programmes without doctoral tracks) and all PhD / Direct-Entry PhD programmes; English IELTS 6.0 (MS) / 6.5 (PhD) or listed TOEFL/Duolingo equivalents; next application window 1 Nov - 15 Dec 2026', official_url = 'https://cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/admission/kfupm-scholarship', source_url = 'https://cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/admission/kfupm-scholarship', verification_status = 'verified', last_verified_at = now() WHERE id = 598 RETURNING id;

